To extract text from a document using JavaScript, you can use various libraries and APIs depending on the type of document (e.g., PDF, Word, HTML). Below is an example of how to extract text from an HTML document using plain JavaScript.

If you need to extract text from other types of documents like PDF or DOCX, you would typically use specialized libraries such as `pdf.js` for PDFs or `mammoth` for DOCX files.

Here's a simple example of extracting text from an HTML document:

```javascript
function extractTextFromHTML(html) {
    // Create a temporary div element
    const tempDiv = document.createElement('div');

    // Set the innerHTML of the temporary div to the provided HTML content
    tempDiv.innerHTML = html;

    // Extract all text nodes within the temporary div
    let textContent = '';
    const walker = document.createTreeWalker(tempDiv, NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT);
    while (walker.nextNode()) {
        textContent += walker.currentNode.nodeValue + ' ';
    }

    return textContent.trim();
}

