</ul>
</body>
</html>
`;

console.log(extractTextFromHTML(htmlContent));
```

This function creates a temporary `div` element, sets its `innerHTML` to the provided HTML content, and then uses a tree walker to traverse through all text nodes in the document, concatenating their values into a single string.

